Package: voltage_explorer
Type: rave-pipeline
Title: Explore 'iEEG' Voltage Responses with Canonical Response Parameterization
Version: 0.0.1
Language: en-US
Encoding: UTF-8
License: MIT
Authors@R: c(
    person("Zhengjia", "Wang", email = "dipterix.wang@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
    )
Description:
    Explore event-related voltage responses of 'iEEG' signals. Users can
    remove drift, down-sample, apply low-pass, high-pass, band-pass, and
    band-stop filters, correct the baseline, and compare the responses across
    condition groups. For each electrode and condition group, the module
    estimates the response duration, onset, amplitude, explained variance,
    and signal-to-noise ratio with the canonical response parameterization
    ('CRP'; Miller et al., 2023, <doi:10.1371/journal.pcbi.1011105>), and
    shows them in plots, a results table, and the 3D brain viewer. Results
    can be exported as an 'HTML' report. This module is part of 'RAVE' and
    can run offline as a pipeline instance; see
    'ravepipeline::pipeline("voltage_explorer")'.
BugReports: https://github.com/orgs/rave-ieeg/discussions
